---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About CalcForDIY — Free Home Improvement Calculators"
  description="CalcForDIY is a free collection of 100 calculators for DIY home improvement projects, built by tradespeople and homeowners to eliminate guesswork at the hardware store."
>
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    <a href="/" class="hover:text-blue-600">Home</a>
    <span>/</span>
    <span>About</span>
  </div>

  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">About CalcForDIY</h1>

  <div class="prose max-w-3xl text-gray-700 space-y-5">

    <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-6 mb-8">
      <p class="text-blue-900 text-lg font-medium mb-0">CalcForDIY is a free collection of <strong>100 calculators</strong> built for homeowners, DIY enthusiasts, and contractors who need fast, accurate material estimates for home improvement projects.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Why We Built This</h2>
    <p>
      Every DIY project starts with the same frustrating question: <em>"How much do I need to buy?"</em> You measure your room, drive to the hardware store, stare at a wall of products, and either buy too much (wasting money) or too little (making a second trip). We built CalcForDIY to eliminate that guesswork entirely.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every calculator on this site runs entirely in your browser. Nothing is uploaded to a server. No account is required. No hidden fees. You enter your measurements, and you get an instant, printable material list.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">What We Cover</h2>
    <p>Our calculators span 8 comprehensive trade categories:</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3 my-4">
      <a href="/calculators#tile-flooring" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-3 text-center hover:border-blue-400 hover:shadow-xs transition-all">
        <div class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm">Tile &amp; Flooring</div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">Tile, grout, thinset, hardwood, laminate</div>
      </a>
      <a href="/calculators#carpentry-framing-roofing" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-3 text-center hover:border-blue-400 hover:shadow-xs transition-all">
        <div class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm">Carpentry &amp; Roofing</div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">Framing, rafters, shingles, decks, stairs</div>
      </a>
      <a href="/calculators#millwork-trim-walls" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-3 text-center hover:border-blue-400 hover:shadow-xs transition-all">
        <div class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm">Millwork &amp; Trim</div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">Crown molding, wainscoting, shiplap</div>
      </a>
      <a href="/calculators#concrete-masonry" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-3 text-center hover:border-blue-400 hover:shadow-xs transition-all">
        <div class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm">Concrete &amp; Masonry</div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">Slabs, Sonotubes, rebar, retaining walls</div>
      </a>
      <a href="/calculators#landscaping-hardscaping" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-3 text-center hover:border-blue-400 hover:shadow-xs transition-all">
        <div class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm">Landscaping &amp; Paving</div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">Gravel driveway, pavers, mulch, French drain</div>
      </a>
      <a href="/calculators#paint-finishing" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-3 text-center hover:border-blue-400 hover:shadow-xs transition-all">
        <div class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm">Paint &amp; Finishing</div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">Interior room, textured wall, exterior</div>
      </a>
      <a href="/calculators#electrical-solar-lighting" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-3 text-center hover:border-blue-400 hover:shadow-xs transition-all">
        <div class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm">Electrical &amp; Solar</div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">EV chargers, subpanels, lighting, solar</div>
      </a>
      <a href="/calculators#plumbing-hvac-energy" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-3 text-center hover:border-blue-400 hover:shadow-xs transition-all">
        <div class="font-semibold text-gray-900 text-sm">Plumbing &amp; HVAC</div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">Sump pump, mini-splits, insulation, heat</div>
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Technical Editorial &amp; Review Board</h2>
    <p>
      To ensure every tool provides safe, code-compliant, and job-site accurate estimates, our calculation engines and guides undergo strict multi-disciplinary review by experienced construction and engineering professionals:
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 my-6 not-prose">
      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-4 shadow-xs">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm mb-3">
          DM
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-base">David Miller, PE</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-blue-600 font-semibold mb-2">Structural &amp; Civil Engineering Consultant</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
          Over 20 years of residential structural design, IRC framing verification, retaining wall stability analysis, and concrete load engineering.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-4 shadow-xs">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-amber-100 text-amber-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm mb-3">
          MV
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-base">Marcus Vance</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-amber-600 font-semibold mb-2">Master Electrician &amp; Solar Specialist</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
          Specialist in NEC (NFPA 70) 2020/2023 compliance, residential subpanel load calculations, EV charger circuit sizing, and voltage drop mitigation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-4 shadow-xs">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm mb-3">
          ER
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-base">Elena Rostova, CBO</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-emerald-600 font-semibold mb-2">Certified Building Official &amp; Cost Estimator</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
          Expert in RSMeans residential construction benchmarking, regional location labor multipliers, and TCNA/NWFA architectural finish standards.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Our Sources &amp; Methodology</h2>
    <p>
      Accuracy matters. If a calculator tells you to buy 4 bags of grout and you actually need 6, that is a failed tool. Every formula on CalcForDIY is sourced from published industry standards:
    </p>
    <ul class="space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Tile Council of North America (TCNA)</strong> — tile waste factors, grout coverage rates, and thinset consumption standards.</li>
      <li><strong>National Wood Flooring Association (NWFA)</strong> — hardwood and laminate waste factor guidelines by room complexity and installation pattern.</li>
      <li><strong>Manufacturer Technical Data Sheets</strong> — from Mapei, LATICRETE, Quikrete, and other major brands for product-specific coverage rates.</li>
      <li><strong>International Residential Code (IRC)</strong> — for framing stud spacing, structural load requirements, and stair geometry.</li>
      <li><strong>National Electrical Code (NEC / NFPA 70)</strong> — for branch circuit sizing, wire gauge ampacity, and continuous load factors.</li>
      <li><strong>Illuminating Engineering Society (IES)</strong> — for recommended foot-candle levels by room type used in our lighting calculators.</li>
      <li><strong>U.S. Energy Information Administration (EIA)</strong> — for average utility rates used as default values in our energy cost calculators.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      For a complete mathematical breakdown of our formulas and safety factors, visit our dedicated <a href="/methodology" class="text-blue-600 font-semibold hover:underline">Calculation Methodology &amp; Standards page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Contact Us &amp; Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Have a question, found a bug, or want to suggest a new calculator? We welcome feedback from homeowners and trade professionals alike.
    </p>
    <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-5">
      <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Email</p>
      <p><a href="mailto:invictusetfortis@gmail.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">invictusetfortis@gmail.com</a></p>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-4">
      We typically respond within 1-2 business days. For calculator suggestions or trade formula submissions, please include the specific code reference or use case you have in mind so we can evaluate it quickly.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>